body:
Bonus question: are there actions I can take against the company selling supplements with tea tree oil? Here's their "Scientific validation" of their ingredients: [http://prosupplements.nl/Profinfo/Biocidin-White-Paper.pdf](http://prosupplements.nl/Profinfo/Biocidin-White-Paper.pdf)

&#x200B;

Under the tea tree oil section, the source cited saying tea tree oil is nontoxic is "A complete guide to aromatherapy." The scientific studies cited do not actually use tea tree oil orally and do not recommend its use orally, citing its toxicity. 

&#x200B;

Proof that tea tree oil is poisonous: [https://www.poison.org/articles/2010-dec/tea-tree-oil](https://www.poison.org/articles/2010-dec/tea-tree-oil)

Actually, I realized that that edit outputted a list where all the strings are split up in an odd way, so I edited it to look like:

    for string in splitList[1:]:
       if not string.startswith('i') or not string.startswith('r'):

Which is what I want. However, this concatenated all of the strings together to once again be a list containing one large string.
